174
00:14:36,107 --> 00:14:42,789
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, the Suttas describe it five hindrances, because that's all, but I'm sure not all the monks will necessarily see them back in the day.

175
00:14:42,849 --> 00:14:46,411
[SPEAKER_01]: They had probably their own ways, but what they all had in common was the pressure.

176
00:14:46,711 --> 00:14:47,491
[SPEAKER_01]: So, where would...

177
00:14:48,215 --> 00:14:49,375
[SPEAKER_01]: Where would you find that pressure?

178
00:14:49,876 --> 00:14:55,977
[SPEAKER_01]: So, where would you find if there is a presence of pressure or possibility of the pressure increasing and so on?

179
00:14:56,237 --> 00:14:56,958
[SPEAKER_01]: Where do you look for it?

180
00:14:57,038 --> 00:14:58,358
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is the level for that?

181
00:14:59,518 --> 00:14:59,959
[SPEAKER_01]: Feelings.

182
00:15:00,039 --> 00:15:00,399
[SPEAKER_01]: Feelings.

183
00:15:00,439 --> 00:15:00,839
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

184
00:15:01,619 --> 00:15:06,601
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you would know that if there is a feeling, to the degree that there is a feeling, to that degree there is a pressure.

185
00:15:07,801 --> 00:15:08,421
[SPEAKER_02]: Any feeling.

186
00:15:08,781 --> 00:15:09,241
[SPEAKER_01]: Any feeling.

187
00:15:09,461 --> 00:15:09,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

188
00:15:09,942 --> 00:15:10,422
[SPEAKER_01]: Any feeling.

189
00:15:10,602 --> 00:15:10,782
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

190
00:15:12,142 --> 00:15:14,143
[SPEAKER_01]: So, pleasant feeling, that's a pressure.

191
00:15:15,478 --> 00:15:16,780
[SPEAKER_01]: Unpleasant feeling, that's a pressure.

192
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:18,342
[SPEAKER_01]: Neutral feeling, that's pressure, yeah.

193
00:15:19,343 --> 00:15:21,426
[SPEAKER_01]: Pressure, then, when known, it's not unpleasant.

194
00:15:22,828 --> 00:15:24,250
[SPEAKER_01]: When not known, it's unpleasant.

195
00:15:26,072 --> 00:15:31,058
[SPEAKER_01]: But fundamentally, there is always a pressure for as long... Well, for as long as you're not an arahant.

196
00:15:31,179 --> 00:15:33,121
[SPEAKER_01]: Obviously, it's not always the same degree of pressure.

197
00:15:33,913 --> 00:15:40,618
[SPEAKER_01]: For somebody whose mind is free, partially free, and so on, he's obviously going to have less things pressuring him, because there are less fetters there.

198
00:15:41,219 --> 00:15:48,704
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, you need to recognize that, oh, it's not like, oh, I'm free from pressure now, and I'm not an arahant.

199
00:15:48,764 --> 00:15:49,525
[SPEAKER_01]: That's impossible.

200
00:15:50,886 --> 00:15:54,349
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's always going to be a degree of feeling, to that extent, there is a degree of pressure.

201
00:15:54,769 --> 00:15:58,592
[SPEAKER_01]: To that extent, there is a potential for hindrance.

202
00:15:58,972 --> 00:16:02,335
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't see that pressure on the level that it exists,

203
00:16:03,555 --> 00:16:16,323
[SPEAKER_01]: As a phenomenon, neither inside nor outside, neither in my head nor in the world, but here, real as such, I mean, the most real thing, directs your whole existence, shapes your whole life decisions and everything else, emotional needs and so on, and pressures.

204
00:16:16,923 --> 00:16:19,625
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't see it on that level, that's where it starts to hinder you.

205
00:16:20,005 --> 00:16:22,026
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where its counterpart starts to hinder you.

206
00:16:24,107 --> 00:16:28,350
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you see it as a pressure, it cannot.

207
00:16:28,490 --> 00:16:30,611
[SPEAKER_01]: It's held, it's basically put in place.

208
00:16:31,412 --> 00:16:32,713
[SPEAKER_01]: It's recognized for what it is,

209
00:16:33,722 --> 00:16:41,648
[SPEAKER_01]: The beautiful, the ugly, the lack of energy, restlessness... Again, like, natural phenomenon in a way.

210
00:16:41,768 --> 00:16:46,852
[SPEAKER_01]: But they don't need to... they hinder you when you are not developed in regard to their pressure.

211
00:16:47,532 --> 00:16:50,734
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're developed in regard to their pressure, they cease to be hindrances.

212
00:16:50,854 --> 00:16:57,099
[SPEAKER_01]: But those things that were hindering you, those contents, those objects, they do remain.

213
00:16:58,852 --> 00:16:59,612
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, there's a sutta.

214
00:16:59,672 --> 00:17:00,913
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't remember the reference now.

215
00:17:01,113 --> 00:17:02,494
[SPEAKER_01]: Maybe I can...

216
00:17:02,514 --> 00:17:03,574
[SPEAKER_01]: It describes exactly that.

217
00:17:03,734 --> 00:17:08,336
[SPEAKER_01]: When rightly attended, they cease to be the hindrance, but they remain that which they were before.

218
00:17:08,497 --> 00:17:09,097
[SPEAKER_01]: They hindered you.

219
00:17:09,882 --> 00:17:12,282
[SPEAKER_01]: But, obviously, you don't start unhindered.

220
00:17:12,402 --> 00:17:17,943
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't start by having a pure sign of beauty that then develops into sensuality.

221
00:17:17,963 --> 00:17:18,544
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no, no, no.

222
00:17:19,084 --> 00:17:21,784
[SPEAKER_01]: Mind not free from hindrances starts with sensuality.

223
00:17:22,384 --> 00:17:30,806
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can only undo the degree of that sensuality and then discover that there is a pure sign of beauty, a pure sign of agreeable.

224
00:17:31,846 --> 00:17:36,247
[SPEAKER_01]: But, attended rightly, cannot bring lust to increase in you.

225
00:17:36,627 --> 00:17:37,167
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible.

226
00:17:37,951 --> 00:17:38,953
[SPEAKER_01]: Attended rightly to what?

227
00:17:39,013 --> 00:17:43,220
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, to that sign, to that pressure, to its characteristics and its core.

228
00:17:47,628 --> 00:17:51,535
[SPEAKER_02]: I think, yeah, it's kind of about seeing what genuinely

229
00:17:54,004 --> 00:18:05,508
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, it's again...

230
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:10,609
[SPEAKER_01]: If you think you should do what you're supposed to do, you're not looking for the pressure.

231
00:18:10,629 --> 00:18:14,531
[SPEAKER_01]: You're just acting out to get rid of the discomfort, which is exactly what hindrance wants you to do.

232
00:18:14,711 --> 00:18:15,591
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the whole point.

233
00:18:18,181 --> 00:18:20,523
[SPEAKER_01]: Indriyas doesn't care if you follow through and how far you go.

234
00:18:20,683 --> 00:18:23,385
[SPEAKER_01]: As long as you act out of the pressure, that's all that matters.

235
00:18:23,805 --> 00:18:25,566
[SPEAKER_00]: You're already caught, you're already hindered.

236
00:18:27,348 --> 00:18:30,870
[SPEAKER_01]: How far you go and whether you get your gratification or not, that's all irrelevant.

237
00:18:31,371 --> 00:18:33,312
[SPEAKER_00]: That's only important to you because you're already caught.

238
00:18:35,554 --> 00:18:46,722
[SPEAKER_00]: If you were to see that pressure as a phenomenon, like you were describing just now, correctly, there would not be... that pressure would not be felt.

239
00:18:48,340 --> 00:18:56,065
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you think you see it rightly as a phenomenon, but there is still that pressure, you are overlooking something.

240
00:18:56,285 --> 00:19:00,568
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and that's the practice there, because initially, naturally, you emphasize your view.

241
00:19:01,089 --> 00:19:05,111
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where the views are kind of the most blameworthy thing, or the best thing that can free you.

242
00:19:06,232 --> 00:19:16,439
[SPEAKER_01]: See, like, you have a criteria whereby, when the pressure is seen rightly, it ceases to pressure you, but it might not feel right to you.

243
00:19:18,523 --> 00:19:26,891
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you still emphasize that, oh, it doesn't feel right, I need to see it again until it feels right, that's already your view being put first.

244
00:19:26,911 --> 00:19:27,132
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

245
00:19:27,252 --> 00:19:28,993
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already under the pressure.

246
00:19:29,734 --> 00:19:38,523
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's where that kind of intelligence and understanding and discernment start to sort of play the part, where you recognize, okay,

247
00:19:39,738 --> 00:19:40,919
[SPEAKER_01]: I know what's right, though.

248
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:49,727
[SPEAKER_01]: I understood that rightly seeing pressure means not being pressured, there and then, while the pressure remains.

249
00:19:49,947 --> 00:19:51,929
[SPEAKER_01]: That which pressures you remains, let's say that way.

250
00:19:52,729 --> 00:20:03,339
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I just need to abstain and refrain from overly defining it so to slot and fit what I expect it fitting to be.

251
00:20:04,621 --> 00:20:17,284
[SPEAKER_01]: And just, pretty much out of faith, stick to the right level, because you recognize, well, but hold on, my goal is not to satisfy my intellectual need for clarity and fit, but my goal is to be free from suffering.

252
00:20:18,404 --> 00:20:30,346
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I've come halfway up, and there is freedom from suffering to that degree, at that extent, but now I kind of carry on more, to fit it even better, in a satisfactory manner.

253
00:20:31,066 --> 00:20:34,167
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like, but if I don't do that, I still have nothing to lose.

254
00:20:36,404 --> 00:20:53,480
[SPEAKER_01]: If I don't give in to that pressure, to overly clarify freedom from doubt and this hindrance and that hindrance, but actually just stay with where the pressure is, recognize it to the extent that I'm not pressured towards things that it wants me to go, it's like, yeah, I have nothing to lose there.

255
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:59,205
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, it's uncomfortable only because of your need to kind of overly do it, overshoot the mark.

256
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:07,150
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's when I was going to ask you, like, what body posture are you now?

257
00:21:08,771 --> 00:21:09,111
[SPEAKER_01]: Sitting.

258
00:21:09,412 --> 00:21:11,593
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, did you have to stop and think about it?

259
00:21:11,613 --> 00:21:12,373
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you have to get up?

260
00:21:12,853 --> 00:21:13,714
[SPEAKER_01]: You already know that.

261
00:21:15,255 --> 00:21:24,040
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like, sometimes when there is too much of a desire to, like, figure it out and understand, you stop seeing the obvious, that is still there, such as body.

262
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:27,622
[SPEAKER_01]: It's still there, even if you don't explicitly think about it.

263
00:21:28,983 --> 00:21:33,046
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's to learn how to keep seeing it without explicitly thinking about it.

264
00:21:33,227 --> 00:21:33,807
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the point.

265
00:21:35,268 --> 00:21:45,977
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the body postures that you can contemplate, or the nature of the body, the universal nature of the organs, regardless of the situation, regardless of the emotional and so on.

266
00:21:46,318 --> 00:21:47,619
[SPEAKER_01]: Because those things would set in.

267
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:51,282
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then they become that which your body is.

268
00:21:51,402 --> 00:21:52,543
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how you see it correctly.

269
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:54,830
[SPEAKER_01]: But the body is already there.

270
00:21:54,890 --> 00:22:01,632
[SPEAKER_01]: The whole, the way of attending to this here and now, it's already on the basis of body being in a certain position here and now.

271
00:22:01,652 --> 00:22:03,273
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, it cannot be elsewhere.

272
00:22:04,293 --> 00:22:14,556
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's more like you undoing that expectation to find the body only after you think about it on your own terms, because it's already there.

273
00:22:14,956 --> 00:22:20,818
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like, I can think about it to find it, or I can refrain from thinking and look, it's already there.

274
00:22:22,750 --> 00:22:24,631
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, that's the direction that everything else goes.

275
00:22:25,212 --> 00:22:29,374
[SPEAKER_01]: First, yeah, you need to pick it up with your craving, to know what to look for.

276
00:22:29,895 --> 00:22:37,340
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, if you're doing it rightly, time recognizes, oh, I'll find it by not actually actively engaging with this craving in that direction.

277
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:41,843
[SPEAKER_01]: But, yeah, pick it up, so I know what to recognize, but recognition is over there.

278
00:22:49,885 --> 00:23:07,472
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, what I found, one kind of good way of putting it, is what Venerable Aniga wrote in that essay regarding yoniso, manasikāra, is that even the recognition of the body already there, is because the body is already there.

279
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:07,732
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

280
00:23:08,812 --> 00:23:15,975
[SPEAKER_01]: So, like, if you understand that, then basically... Well, it's it's the question of understanding it once.

281
00:23:16,155 --> 00:23:18,436
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a question of training yourself to keep seeing it that way.

282
00:23:21,988 --> 00:23:38,558
[SPEAKER_02]: So, like, let's say, you do, you are able to endure things on the right level, to the extent that the pressure is not felt, at least once or something.

283
00:23:39,679 --> 00:23:43,101
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, is there something else you need to do?

284
00:23:44,602 --> 00:23:51,546
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you just need to make sure that you always stay above those pressures, then.

285
00:23:53,096 --> 00:24:02,620
[SPEAKER_02]: But there's not... as in, I don't... there's nothing... there's not really more you need to kind of do on top of that.

286
00:24:02,860 --> 00:24:07,943
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, there is, but that can become only apparent once you're thoroughly above the pressures.

287
00:24:08,583 --> 00:24:11,664
[SPEAKER_01]: Because... but yeah, the suttas do say what you need to do.

288
00:24:11,904 --> 00:24:17,527
[SPEAKER_01]: When you get established in not being moved by any pressure, when it's completely equanimous,

289
00:24:18,675 --> 00:24:21,898
[SPEAKER_01]: Peaceful, immovable, quite delightful.

290
00:24:22,699 --> 00:24:25,341
[SPEAKER_01]: Now you regard that the same way as you did the precious.

291
00:24:26,442 --> 00:24:31,927
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, this is also a debt, a boil, a dart, affliction.

292
00:24:32,387 --> 00:24:34,910
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm better off even not having this.

293
00:24:35,770 --> 00:24:38,173
[SPEAKER_01]: So then your mind turns away even from that first jhāna.

294
00:24:39,414 --> 00:24:42,396
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where the whole āsava, all of the āsavas will have to be uprooted.

295
00:24:42,817 --> 00:24:43,898
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing can remain lingering.

296
00:24:45,358 --> 00:24:53,082
[SPEAKER_01]: But, in order to do that, yeah, first establish yourself in the entire piece, then no hindrance can move you, and then this will kind of...

297
00:24:54,122 --> 00:25:00,145
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, I wouldn't say it would come naturally, but with all the suttas that we already know, there is no way that then you would not... Oh, hold on.

298
00:25:00,185 --> 00:25:01,245
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, this too, actually.

299
00:25:02,086 --> 00:25:02,906
[SPEAKER_01]: It would be better if...

300
00:25:05,341 --> 00:25:08,364
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it would be better if it were not there to begin with, certainly.

301
00:25:08,864 --> 00:25:12,928
[SPEAKER_01]: Because any experience that arises is not worth clinging to.

302
00:25:13,188 --> 00:25:16,611
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not worth having, it's not worth delighting or finding safety in.

303
00:25:17,132 --> 00:25:25,339
[SPEAKER_01]: Even this pure, purified, freed experience from all the pressures, all the compulsions, all the hindrances, all the doubts and everything else.

304
00:25:27,541 --> 00:25:29,003
[SPEAKER_00]: Not mine, not for me, not I am.

305
00:25:34,967 --> 00:25:41,788
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that experience of being free from pressures, hindrances, is real as such.

306
00:25:42,368 --> 00:25:43,669
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a phenomenon enduring there.

307
00:25:51,150 --> 00:25:56,011
[SPEAKER_01]: Phenomenon where the directionality of affirming or denying is completely evened out.

308
00:25:56,611 --> 00:25:58,731
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's completely even.

309
00:25:59,571 --> 00:26:01,372
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no more leaning forward nor against.

310
00:26:02,332 --> 00:26:03,512
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's still real as such.

311
00:26:06,102 --> 00:26:07,563
[SPEAKER_01]: The middle ground is real as such.

312
00:26:09,185 --> 00:26:18,732
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you see it, means, oh, you will know it as impermanent, unownable, rightly developed, but equally not worth owning either.

